  "implementationPrompt": {
    "title": "CNXRetail UI implementation brief",
    "prompt": "Implement the CNXRetail dashboard using this JSONC design system as the authoritative visual specification. Recreate the supplied reference screenshot's warm amber and cream identity, left navigation sidebar, amber company header, financial metric cards, payment status visualization, overlapping payment cards, recent transaction list and full-width invoice table. Match the reference's visual hierarchy, proportions, spacing, alignment, typography, radii, borders and restrained use of shadows. Support both light and dark themes using the semantic theme values defined here; preserve amber as the brand colour and use layered charcoal surfaces for dark mode. Follow the responsive breakpoints and behaviours defined here: use a navigation drawer on mobile, reorganize analytics into a single column when necessary, simplify transaction rows, and convert the invoice table into stacked cards on narrow screens. Build reusable components and apply the same design language to Home, Products, Tasks, Accounts, Contacts, Invoices, Payments and Documents. Treat the two core palettes as the only brand palettes. Use neutrals for structure and semantic accents only for statuses and feedback. Do not introduce unrelated colours, heavy shadows, decorative gradients or a different visual direction. Prioritize fidelity to the screenshot, consistency across modules, readability of financial data, accessible interaction states and responsive usability."
  }
